The inscricoes.spec.js test uses `X-Usuario: org-ana` for the cancelamento request. And it works! So somehow the auth is being set up even though the middleware should skip it for `/atividades/` paths.

Let me think about why this works. Maybe the middleware check `req.path.startsWith('/atividades/')` doesn't match the actual path being tested? Or maybe there's something about how the test runs that's different.

Actually, wait. Let me re-read the middleware code very carefully:

```javascript
if (req.path === '/salas' || req.path === '/atividades' || req.path.startsWith('/atividades/')) {
    return next();
}
```

The check is `req.path.startsWith('/atividades/')`. The path `/atividades/atv_1a2b3c4d/cancelamento` does start with `/atividades/`, so it should be skipped.

But the tests work... Maybe I'm missing something. Let me just try running the inscricoes test to see if it actually works:

